# The canon: fixed frames that say what the game looks like. tools/canon.sh shoots
# them (seed 7) and lays them beside the accepted set on one contact sheet.
#
# Every frame here is pinned. The canon is a REFERENCE: two runs at the same
# commit must differ only where the game changed, so nothing in it may be left
# to what the weather rules roll at the minute the frame happens to be taken.
# `weather clear:0` holds for the rest of the run (Weather.force), and the two
# frames that are about rain ask for rain and then give the clear sky back.
# (Playtest wave A finding 9: the snowfield frames moved 4.14 between two runs
# at one commit, against a tolerance of 3, because its climate rolls whiteouts
# and a whiteout over white ground moves a great many pixels.)
weather clear:0
place spawn
wait 0.8
shot 01-spawn-morning
place coast
wait 0.8
shot 02-coast with land:coast
place moss
wait 0.8
shot 03-moss with land:moss
place pinewood
wait 0.8
shot 04-pinewood with land:pinewood
place snowfield
wait 0.8
shot 05-snowfield with land:snowfield
place bonelands
wait 0.8
shot 06-bonelands with land:bonelands
place burning
wait 0.8
shot 07-burning with land:burning
place coast-pinewood
wait 0.8
shot 08-eco-coast-pinewood
place pinewood-snowfield
wait 0.8
shot 09-eco-pinewood-snowfield
place bonelands-burning
wait 0.8
shot 10-eco-bonelands-burning
place coast-moss
wait 0.8
shot 11-eco-coast-moss
place spawn
wait 0.8
hour 19.5
wait 0.4
shot 12-spawn-dusk
hour 23
wait 0.4
shot 13-spawn-night
tap lamp
wait 0.4
shot 14-night-lamp with lamp
hour 12
place snowfield
wait 0.8
wait 0.3
shot 15-snowfield-noon with land:snowfield
place burning
wait 0.8
hour 20
wait 0.3
shot 16-burning-dusk with land:burning

# The two things the canon never showed: wet ground mirroring light, and the
# stolen neon somebody wired into a house. The neon frame goes to the landmark
# where a shack wired the machines' light into its wall (GenWorks records it, and
# `place` fails if the world has none), and then asks the picture itself whether
# a tube is in it: the frame used to be shot at the spawn village, where the
# canon seed has no neon shack at all, so the reference for "stolen neon" held
# none of the three tube colours and could not have caught a regression in them.
place spawn
wait 0.8
hour 22
weather rain:1
wait 1.2
shot 17-village-wet-night
place stolen_light
zoom 9
wait 1.2
walk 0,1 1.2
wait 0.6
shot 18-stolen-neon-close with pixels:4df2ff+ff40cc+8cff59:60
zoom 14
weather clear:0
